cabal-version:      2.4
name:               casa-reoc
version:            0.1.0.0
license:            BSD-3-Clause
license-file:       LICENCE
author:             Tony Morris <ʇǝu˙sıɹɹoɯʇ@ןןǝʞsɐɥ> <dibblego>
maintainer:         Tony Morris <ʇǝu˙sıɹɹoɯʇ@ןןǝʞsɐɥ> <dibblego>
copyright:          Copyright (c) 2026 System F Aerial Operations Pty Ltd
synopsis:           The documents of a CASA ReOC application, as Haskell data types
category:           Aviation
description:
  <<https://logo.systemf.com.au/systemf-450x450.png>>
  .
  The variables of an application to CASA for the initial issue of a
  remotely piloted aircraft operator's certificate (ReOC), of its RPAS
  operations manual and of its RePL training manual, as data types with
  classy optics. A value of @ReOC@ gives a filled CASA Form 101-02 (XFDF), a
  complete operations manual and, with RePL training, a RePL training manual
  (Flat ODF text).
  .
  == Data types
  .
  Every data type is in its own module under @ReOC.Data@, and every name of a
  field or constructor in its own module under @ReOC.Name@, following the
  classy optics recipe. Values that have an invariant (an ABN, a phone
  number, text that is not blank) are primitive types under
  @ReOC.Primitive@, built with a prism or a literal checked at compile time.
  .
  == Documents
  .
  @ReOC.Render.ApplicationForm@ gives the XFDF of CASA Form 101-02,
  @ReOC.Render.OperationsManual@ the operations manual and
  @ReOC.Render.TrainingManual@ the RePL training manual. @ReOC.Render.Write@
  writes them into a directory. The internal library @examples@ holds the
  applications of four made-up operators.

